# Copy to register/.env and adjust. Not committed — .env is gitignored.

# Where the form POSTs. Same-origin by default: Caddy publishes the API under
# /api on the register host, so no CORS is involved.
#
# The *client* reads a variable of the same name, out of its own .env, for the
# case where it plays a world that published no domain — a world with one is
# worked out from that (register.<domain>/api/register) and needs neither.
VITE_REGISTER_API=/api/register

# Where the OZT/OZJ interface sprites are fetched from. The register page needs
# four files out of Data/Interface, so it borrows the client's published tree
# instead of shipping its own copy. Cross-origin — the client host must send
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin for this (see README).
#
# Leave unset to serve a local ./Data/ next to the register build instead.
VITE_DATA_URL=https://play.ignies.net/Data/
